<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gadayuddha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 982</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Sahasabhimavijaya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gadayuddha ('battle of maces') is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> poem by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranna">Ranna</a>, composed around 982, that retells the final duel between Bhima and Duryodhana from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>. Written in the champu style, it compares its patron, the Western Chalukya prince Satyashraya, to Bhima and is counted among the masterpieces of early Kannada literature.</p></div>
